{
  "id": "Compound::DB00962 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Zaleplon, through a series of causal relationships, is linked to Cyp3a4 via Colchicine and Fenofibrate. The evidence suggests that Zaleplon causes Lactose Intolerance or Lactase Deficiency, both of which are subsequently caused by Colchicine. Colchicine binds to Cyp3a4, establishing a direct interaction between Colchicine and the enzyme. Similarly, Fenofibrate, which is caused by Cataract Specified, binds to Cyp3a4. While the exact mechanism by which Zaleplon influences Colchicine or Fenofibrate remains unclear, the shared pathway through Colchicine and Fenofibrate provides a consistent route to Cyp3a4. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Zaleplon in modulating Cyp3a4 through the action of Colchicine or Fenofibrate, though the precise nature of this interaction requires further investigation.",
